<v Woman 2>好吧。

00:21:03.060 --> 00:21:05.400
<v Man>The Jews--
<v Man>犹太人——

00:21:05.400 --> 00:21:09.450
<v Woman 2>This is never good.
<v Woman 2>这准没好事。

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:10.450
<v Man>Scene!
<v Man>场景结束！

00:21:10.450 --> 00:21:18.210
<v Man>[AUDIENCE CHEERING]
<v Man>[观众欢呼]

00:21:18.210 --> 00:21:21.660
<v Woman>I was just going to tell a quick story.
<v Woman>我原本打算讲个短故事。

00:21:21.660 --> 00:21:22.830
<v Man>I'm going to listen.
<v Man>我会听的。

00:21:22.830 --> 00:21:49.310
<v Woman>Great. Well, I feel like we keep talking about, like, especially people who were always experiencing a Jewish Christmas experience. But I was the exact opposite, where until I was 13 years old, I did not know Jewish people existed maybe. And I loved Christmas so much that I would get up at 3:00 in the morning to try and look at my presents.
<v Woman>太棒了。嗯，我觉得我们一直在谈论，特别是那些一直有犹太圣诞经历的人。但我刚好相反，我在13岁之前，甚至可能不知道犹太人的存在。我太喜欢圣诞节了，以至于我会在凌晨3点起床去看我的礼物。

00:21:49.310 --> 00:22:28.210
<v Woman>And I just always felt like such simple things would give me such overwhelming joy that I wish I could have that now. Like, one Christmas morning I was in my little Christmas gown, and I crept down, and there was a giant stuffed animal Saint Bernard, which is not like a bike that you can ride or something that you can do. It's just going to sit there, and you're going to look at it and love it. And as soon as I saw it, I was so happy I could not believe my eyes. I fell to my knees and I [BLEEP] my pants.
<v Woman>我总是觉得简单的东西就能带给我如此巨大的快乐，真希望现在还能有那种感觉。比如，某个圣诞早晨，我穿着我的小圣诞睡袍，悄悄走下楼，那里有一个巨大的填充玩具圣伯纳犬，它不像自行车那样可以骑，或者像其他东西那样可以玩。它只是坐在那里，你只会看着它并爱上它。一看到它，我就开心得不敢相信自己的眼睛。我跪倒在地，然后[哔]了我的裤子。

00:22:28.210 --> 00:22:59.660
<v Woman>I just-- like upon the sight of this Saint Bernard, I just was like, thank you! And I fell to my knees and just blasted right into my pants. So I had to creep into my parents' room and say, like, "Good morning, Mom. Merry Christmas. I've soiled myself, and I need your help."
<v Woman>我只是——看到那个圣伯纳犬的瞬间，我就想，谢谢你！我跪下，然后直接拉在裤子里了。所以我不得不偷偷潜进父母的房间说，“早安，妈妈。圣诞快乐。我把裤子弄脏了，我需要你的帮助。”

00:22:59.660 --> 00:23:16.850
<v Ira Glass>Can I ask the other improv stars on stage, like, did you have moments like that, of such incredible joy at Christmas? Not that would take your body to that length, but do you know what I mean? Like moments of just pure, pure joy in that way that I think we rarely have as adults. Do you have--
<v Ira Glass>我能问问舞台上其他的即兴巨星吗，你们小时候有过那样的时刻吗，在圣诞节感受到难以置信的快乐？不是说会让你身体失控的那种，但你明白我的意思吗？就是那种纯粹的，纯粹的快乐，我想我们成年后很少有那种体验。你们有——

00:23:16.850 --> 00:23:49.870
<v Man>When I was a kid, my sister and I would get up really early and stand at the top of the stairs, because we knew we weren't allowed to go downstairs. And my dad had this tradition. We would have to wait for him to-- we would just shake with anticipation at the top of the stairs, and wait and wait, and bother them, my parents, to get out of bed. And we'd pull them out of bed. And they would take their sweet time putting on their clothes and getting their shaving, just to torture us, because they knew we were at the top of the stairs.
<v Man>当我还是个孩子，我和我姐姐会起得很早，站在楼梯顶端，因为我们知道不能下楼。但我爸爸有个传统。我们要等他——我们在楼梯顶端激动得发抖，一直等啊等，去骚扰他们，我的父母，让他们起床。我们会把他们从床上拽起来。而他们会磨磨蹭蹭地穿衣服、刮胡子，纯粹是为了折磨我们，因为他们知道我们在楼梯顶端。

00:23:49.870 --> 00:24:12.620
<v Man>And my dad would go downstairs first and say, "Let's see if Santa came." Like, he'd look around the hallway and say, "I don't see any evidence that he's been here." And then he'd walk into the dining room, and he would disappear. And we'd hear him go, "Well, mm, no, nothing in here."
<v Man>爸爸会先下楼说，“看看圣诞老人来了没。”他会环顾四周说，“我没看到他来过的迹象。”然后他会走进餐厅，他就消失了。我们听到他说，“嗯，没，这儿什么都没有。”

00:24:12.620 --> 00:24:32.130
<v Man>And we're up there, going like, "It's the dining room. There's nothing in the dining room!" Goes into this kind of side little sitting room and same thing. He disappears. He does the same shtick of "No, nothing in here." And then he'd say-- inevitably, he'd say, "I don't know if he came."
<v Man>我们在楼上喊，“那是餐厅。餐厅里本来就不会有！”他走进旁边的小休息室，也是同样的事。他消失了。他重复同样的把戏：“没，这儿什么都没有。”然后他会说——不可避免地，他说，“不知道他有没有来。”

00:24:32.130 --> 00:24:52.120
<v Man>The first couple years, we were really nervous that maybe Santa did not come. But then after three or four years of this, we were like, "Of course he came. Everything's in the-- go to the family room! Go to the family-- were the tree is, where the fireplace is. Santa's not going to come down and then cart everything into the dining room."
<v Man>前几年，我们真的很紧张，怕圣诞老人没来。但三四年后，我们想，“他当然来了。东西都在——去家庭厅（Family Room）！去家庭厅——那是树所在地，壁炉所在地。圣诞老人不会下楼然后把所有东西搬进餐厅的。”

00:24:52.120 --> 00:24:55.830
<v Girl>Dad, you idiot! Go to the family room!
<v Girl>爸爸，你这个白痴！去家庭厅！

00:24:55.830 --> 00:25:00.100
<v Boy>Family room! Family room! Go to the-- [GROAN]
<v Boy>家庭厅！家庭厅！去——[呻吟]

00:25:00.100 --> 00:25:02.940
<v Dad>Nothing in here.
<v Dad>这儿什么都没有。

00:25:02.940 --> 00:25:07.390
<v Girl>Oh, my god! Dad, I will kill you! Please let us down the stairs!
<v Girl>噢，天哪！爸爸，我要杀了你！请让我们下楼梯！

00:25:07.390 --> 00:25:10.540
<v Dad>Maybe I'll go look up in the attic.
<v Dad>也许我会去阁楼看看。

00:25:10.540 --> 00:25:14.230
<v Boy>What's wrong with you? What's wrong with you? It's not going to be in the attic.
<v Boy>你有什么毛病？你有什么毛病？东西又不会在阁楼。

00:25:14.230 --> 00:25:18.710
<v Mom>Oh, guys. Your dad's having fun. Come on.
<v Mom>噢，孩子们。你们爸爸在找乐子。好了。

00:25:18.710 --> 00:25:22.170
<v Boy>Point your stupid freshly-shaven face towards the family room.
<v Boy>把那张蠢蠢的刚刮过胡子的脸朝向家庭厅吧。

00:25:22.170 --> 00:25:24.480
<v Man>I want to talk to you guys about your dad.
<v Man>我想和你们聊聊你们爸爸。

00:25:24.480 --> 00:25:25.090
<v Boy>OK.
<v Boy>好的。

00:25:25.090 --> 00:25:25.930
<v Man>He has Alzheimer's.
<v Man>他有阿尔茨海默症。

00:25:25.930 --> 00:25:31.370
<v Boy>What?
<v Boy>什么？

00:25:31.370 --> 00:25:35.340
<v Man>He doesn't know where the presents are.
<v Man>他不知道礼物在哪。

00:25:35.340 --> 00:25:41.220
<v Mom>That is true. We've been saying he was having fun, but holy hell.
<v Mom>那是真的。我们一直以为他在开玩笑，但我的天啊。

00:25:41.220 --> 00:25:43.120
<v Woman>Scene!
<v Woman>场景结束！

00:25:43.120 --> 00:25:47.900
<v Woman>[AUDIENCE CHEERING]
<v Woman>[观众欢呼]

00:25:47.900 --> 00:25:50.290
<v Santa>Ho, ho, ho, come in here, elves.
<v Santa>呵呵呵，进来，精灵们。

00:25:50.290 --> 00:25:53.420
<v Elf 1>OK, Mr. Santy Claus.
<v Elf 1>好的，圣诞老人。

00:25:53.420 --> 00:25:59.970
<v Santa>Ho, ho, ho! Merry Christmas.
<v Santa>呵呵呵！圣诞快乐。

00:25:59.970 --> 00:26:03.300
<v Elf 2>Thank you again.
<v Elf 2>再次谢谢你。

00:26:03.300 --> 00:26:09.390
<v Santa>I know you want to tell you something I've never told you about Christmas.
<v Santa>我知道你们想告诉我关于圣诞节我从未告诉过你们的事。

00:26:09.390 --> 00:26:17.330
<v Elf 1>Santa, we've been working for you for 472 years. You're going to have to dig deep in that bag.
<v Elf 1>圣诞老人，我们为你工作了472年了。你得在那袋子里深挖一下。

00:26:17.330 --> 00:26:20.860
<v Santa>Well, I've told you that it's a magical time of year.
<v Santa>嗯，我告诉过你们这是一年中神奇的时刻。

00:26:20.860 --> 00:26:21.670
<v Elf 2>Uh-huh, uh-huh.
<v Elf 2>嗯哼，嗯哼。

00:26:21.670 --> 00:26:27.380
<v Santa>I've told you we give presents to millions of children in the world.
<v Santa>我告诉过你们我们给世界上数百万的孩子送礼物。

00:26:27.380 --> 00:26:27.820
<v Elf 1>Mm-hm.
<v Elf 1>嗯哼。

00:26:27.820 --> 00:26:28.710
<v Elf 2>We know. We make all that stuff.
<v Elf 2>我们知道。那些东西都是我们做的。

00:26:28.710 --> 00:26:32.050
<v Elf 1>Yeah, we do that.
<v Elf 1>对，我们做了那些。

00:26:32.050 --> 00:26:42.960
<v Santa>But I haven't told you Rudolph has cancer. The red nose is--
<v Santa>但我没告诉你们鲁道夫得癌症了。红鼻子是——

00:26:42.960 --> 00:26:49.830
<v Elf 1>Why didn't we get him treated? He's had that red nose for so long.
<v Elf 1>为什么我们没给他治疗？他的红鼻子已经很久了。

00:26:49.830 --> 00:26:53.950
<v Santa>For years, we just thought it was adorable.
<v Santa>多年来，我们一直以为那是可爱的。

00:26:53.950 --> 00:26:56.600
<v Elf 1>I feel so bad we used to laugh and call him names.
<v Elf 1>我真愧疚，我们以前总是嘲笑他并给他起外号。

00:26:56.600 --> 00:27:06.750
<v Man>Scene!
<v Man>场景结束！

00:27:06.750 --> 00:27:19.460
<v Man 1>I have a question. I wonder what you guys think of this. And I think this makes me sound like a bad person. Do you feel like Christmas loses a lot of the joy when you hit an age where you have to start buying presents for other people?
<v Man 1>我有个问题。我想知道你们是怎么想的。我觉得这让我听起来像个坏人。你们觉得当你们到了不得不开始给别人买礼物的年纪，圣诞节的乐趣是否会减少很多？

00:27:19.460 --> 00:27:20.960
<v Man 2>I have not hit that age.
<v Man 2>我还没到那个年纪。

00:27:20.960 --> 00:27:25.920
<v Ira Glass>Really?
<v Ira Glass>真的吗？

00:27:25.920 --> 00:27:27.170
<v Woman>1,000% yes.
<v Woman>1000%同意。

00:27:27.170 --> 00:27:36.130
<v Man 1>I feel like it takes-- it's like a fun magic thing, and then when you actually have to give back to other people, it becomes such a drag. Such a drag.
<v Man 1>我觉得它带走了——它原本是件好玩的神奇事，然后当你真的不得不回报别人时，它就变成了一种负担。真的是负担。

00:27:36.130 --> 00:27:39.250
<v Woman>Your parents didn't make you give presents to your siblings?
<v Woman>你父母没让你给兄弟姐妹送礼物？

00:27:39.250 --> 00:28:09.400
<v Man 1>To my sibling? Yeah, I had one brother. Our elementary school rent-- did you guys have this? Our elementary school had a thing that was just bad presents. It's like, you'd go into the gym and be like, oh, you can buy your dad a little screwdriver set, or you can buy your mom a plastic ring. It was all the same stuff. So every year, my brother was just an interchangeable-- like, "I got you the neon flyswatter." "Great, I got you the slap bracelet." You know? And our mom would give us the money anyway.
<v Man 1>给兄弟姐妹？有，我有一个兄弟。我们小学卖——你们有过吗？我们小学有个活动就是专门卖烂礼物。就像，你进体育馆，噢，你可以给爸爸买个小螺丝刀套装，或者给妈妈买个塑料戒指。全是一样的货。所以每年，我兄弟和我就是互换——“我给了你这个霓虹苍蝇拍。”“太棒了，我给了你这个啪啪圈。”你知道吗？反正妈妈会给我们钱。

00:28:09.400 --> 00:28:19.140
<v Man 2>This might sound cynical. My wife and I, we don't give each other Christmas presents, because neither of us believe in holidays.
<v Man 2>这听起来可能很愤世嫉俗。我和我妻子，我们不给彼此送圣诞礼物，因为我们都不信这些节日。

00:28:19.140 --> 00:28:20.470
<v Woman>You don't believe in them?
<v Woman>你们不信它们？

00:28:20.470 --> 00:28:21.770
<v Man 2>Well, they're out there.
<v Man 2>嗯，它们就在那儿。

00:28:21.770 --> 00:28:25.790
<v Woman>Like, they exist.
<v Woman>就像，它们存在。

00:28:25.790 --> 00:28:37.310
<v Man 1>Every 4th of July, do you think a war is breaking out?
<v Man 1>每逢7月4日，你觉得战争爆发了吗？

00:28:37.310 --> 00:28:46.870
<v Man 2>No, to Chris's point, neither of us like the pressure of having to get a gift. And we just don't like them. So we're just like, "No, we don't want that in our relationship."
<v Man 2>不，针对克里斯的观点，我们都不喜欢必须送礼物的压力。而且我们都不喜欢礼物。所以我们就像，“不，我们不希望这存在于我们的关系里。”

00:28:46.870 --> 00:29:08.780
<v Man 3>Well, I'm the opposite. When I grew up, I remember the first presents I bought. And it's still essentially true of me now, is that I'm really excited for people to open the present I found or made for them. And watching them open other people's presents makes me angry. And I just am waiting for them to get to my present.
<v Man 3>嗯，我正好相反。我长大时，记得我买的第一份礼物。这直到现在对我来说依然基本适用，就是我真的很兴奋看到人们打开我为他们找到或制作的礼物。看到他们打开别人的礼物反而让我生气。我只是在等他们轮到拆我的礼物。

00:29:08.780 --> 00:29:13.150
<v Man 2>I'm going to walk you back on that one. Are you making a lot of presents?
<v Man 2>我要收回刚才的话。你做了很多礼物？

00:29:13.150 --> 00:29:14.110
<v Man 1>Found or made?
<v Man 1>找到或制作的？

00:29:14.110 --> 00:29:15.460
<v Man 1>Same thing.
<v Man 1>一回事。

00:29:15.460 --> 00:29:16.730
<v Man 3>What is unusual about that?
<v Man 3>那有什么不寻常的吗？

00:29:16.730 --> 00:29:18.250
<v Man 1>You're a really good person.
<v Man 1>你真是个好人。

00:29:18.250 --> 00:29:20.020
<v Boy>Mom, mom.
<v Boy>妈妈，妈妈。

00:29:20.020 --> 00:29:22.000
<v Mom>Oh, sweetie.
<v Mom>噢，宝贝。

00:29:22.000 --> 00:29:25.280
<v Boy>I got this for you.
<v Boy>这是给你的。

00:29:25.280 --> 00:29:27.220
<v Mom>Oh, sweetie.
<v Mom>噢，宝贝。

00:29:27.220 --> 00:29:29.090
<v Boy>It's a paper puppet.
<v Boy>这是一个纸木偶。

00:29:29.090 --> 00:29:31.570
<v Mom>Oh. Oh, honey.
<v Mom>噢。噢，亲爱的。

00:29:31.570 --> 00:29:33.450
<v Boy>It's a paper puppet.
<v Boy>这是一个纸木偶。

00:29:33.450 --> 00:29:34.150
<v Mom>Honey.
<v Mom>亲爱的。

00:29:34.150 --> 00:29:36.610
<v Boy>What did you get me?
<v Boy>你送我什么了？

00:29:36.610 --> 00:29:39.560
<v Mom>You know what? Greg, now is not a good time.
<v Mom>你知道吗？格雷格，现在不是好时候。

00:29:39.560 --> 00:29:40.820
<v Greg>Oh, OK.
<v Greg>噢，好的。

00:29:40.820 --> 00:29:51.780
<v Mom>Sorry. Sweet-- Mom's friend, Greg, he might want a paper puppet to play with, too.
<v Mom>抱歉。亲爱的——妈妈的朋友格雷格，他也可能想玩玩纸木偶。

00:29:51.780 --> 00:29:55.830
<v Greg>Yeah. Yeah, Greg might want a paper puppet.
<v Greg>对。对，格雷格可能也想要个纸木偶。

00:29:55.830 --> 00:30:00.430
<v Boy>I only made one paper puppet.
<v Boy>我只做了一个纸木偶。

00:30:00.430 --> 00:30:07.220
<v Mom>Well, you know what? That's great, honey, because Greg and Mommy are going to share, because sharing is caring.
<v Mom>嗯，你知道吗？那太棒了，亲爱的，因为格雷格和妈咪要分享，因为分享就是关怀。

00:30:07.220 --> 00:30:11.550
<v Boy>Yeah. (SINGING) Sharing is caring.
<v Boy>对。（歌唱）分享就是关怀。

00:30:11.550 --> 00:30:12.430
<v Mom>OK.
<v Mom>好的。

00:30:12.430 --> 00:30:14.410
<v Boy>I want you to share the paper puppet.
<v Boy>我希望你分享那个纸木偶。

00:30:14.410 --> 00:30:17.230
<v Greg>Oh, that's awesome. Yeah, thank you for that. That's nice.
<v Greg>噢，那太棒了。对，谢谢你。真好。

00:30:17.230 --> 00:30:20.660
<v Mom>Greg, you please put on a robe?
<v Mom>格雷格，请你穿上长袍好吗？

00:30:20.660 --> 00:30:22.380
<v Greg>Sure, I guess so.
<v Greg>好的，我想可以吧。

00:30:22.380 --> 00:30:34.190
<v Mom>OK, sweetie, now remember, we said when Greg's over, we're going to knock on the door and we're not going to come in at 3:00. I love my paper puppet. I love my paper puppet, but it's time to go back to bed, OK, sweetie?
<v Mom>好的，亲爱的，现在记得，我们说过格雷格来的时候，我们会敲门，不会在3点钟闯进来。我爱我的纸木偶。我爱我的纸木偶，但该回床上睡觉了，好吗，亲爱的？

00:30:34.190 --> 00:30:35.320
<v Boy>Can I get in bed with you guys?
<v Boy>我能去你们床上吗？

00:30:35.320 --> 00:30:38.640
<v Mom>Not a good time, baby. Not a good time.
<v Mom>现在不是时候，宝贝。现在不是时候。

00:30:38.640 --> 00:30:40.880
<v Greg>And I want to be honest.
<v Greg>而且我想诚实点。

00:30:40.880 --> 00:30:43.750
<v Mom>No, maybe not. Not a good time.
<v Mom>不，也许不行。现在不是时候。

00:30:43.750 --> 00:30:47.950
<v Woman>Scene!
<v Woman>场景结束！

00:30:47.950 --> 00:30:59.980
<v Woman>Wait, so probably not use able, but for my own sake, there's two things that we went past that I want to hear. And one is what Greg was going to say when he said, "Can I be honest with you?"
<v Woman>等等，这可能用不上，但为了我自己的好奇心，有两件事我们跳过了，我想听听。一是格雷格说“我能跟你坦白吗”时原本想说什么。

00:30:59.980 --> 00:31:07.940
<v Man>Greg was going to say, "I'm going to be honest. I didn't get you anything. But your present will be a father figure, if you play your cards right."
<v Man>格雷格原本想说：“我要坦白。我什么都没给你买。但如果你表现得好，你的礼物将是一位父亲形象。”

00:31:07.940 --> 00:31:15.600
<v Man>[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]
<v Man>[观众笑声]

00:31:15.600 --> 00:31:40.760
<v Aidy Bryant>You know what? There was no, like, religious factor in my Christmas experience. But it was all about like creating your own magic, I feel like. Like, we had this family tradition where Christmas Eve, everyone had to do one trick, which could be of any sort. And then if you did your trick, you got to open one present before you went to bed.
<v Aidy Bryant>你知道吗？我的圣诞经历里没什么宗教因素。但我感觉这全关于创造你自己的魔法。就像，我们家有个传统，平安夜每个人必须表演一个把戏，任何类型的都可以。然后如果你表演了把戏，你可以在上床前拆一份礼物。

00:31:40.760 --> 00:31:43.930
<v Man>And now you're a professional performer.
<v Man>现在你成了专业演员。

00:31:43.930 --> 00:31:58.380
<v Aidy Bryant>I know. But you know what? Like, all the tricks-- I mean, it was all kinds of things. Like I remember one year, my aunt and uncle timed like a nostril flashlight dance to dueling banjos. And like--
<v Aidy Bryant>我知道。但你知道吗？那些把戏——我是说，各种各样的东西。我记得有一年，我的姑姑和姨夫配合着《决斗班卓琴》做了一个鼻孔手电筒舞蹈。就像——

00:31:58.380 --> 00:32:01.490
<v Woman>What?
<v Woman>什么？

00:32:01.490 --> 00:32:09.300
<v Jeff>Welcome to the Bryant Family Talent Show. Does anyone want to start?
<v Jeff>欢迎来到布莱恩特家庭才艺秀。有人想开始吗？

00:32:09.300 --> 00:32:11.900
<v Woman>I think, Jeff, we've got a real great lineup.
<v Woman>我觉得，杰夫，我们有非常棒的阵容。

00:32:11.900 --> 00:32:12.550
<v Jeff>Oh, we got a great lineup.
<v Jeff>噢，我们有很棒的阵容。

00:32:12.550 --> 00:32:13.550
<v Woman>We're really excited.
<v Woman>我们真的很兴奋。

00:32:13.550 --> 00:32:19.180
<v Jeff>Great. Big, big, big, big lineup this year.
<v Jeff>很棒。阵容很大很大，今年。

00:32:19.180 --> 00:32:25.850
<v Woman>But I have to say I've been hearing whisperings from Samantha that she's got a real great talent coming up.
<v Woman>但我得说我听到萨曼莎（Samantha）在窃窃私语说她有个很棒的才艺要登场。

00:32:25.850 --> 00:32:27.090
<v Samantha>It's not ready!
<v Samantha>还没准备好！

00:32:27.090 --> 00:32:27.990
<v Woman>Oh!
<v Woman>噢！

00:32:27.990 --> 00:32:29.740
<v Samantha>It's not ready. It's not ready.
<v Samantha>还没准备好。还没准备好。

00:32:29.740 --> 00:32:30.940
<v Woman>OK, sweetie. OK.
<v Woman>好的，亲爱的。好的。

00:32:30.940 --> 00:32:31.690
<v Samantha>Stall, stall!
<v Samantha>拖延，拖延！

00:32:31.690 --> 00:32:33.680
<v Woman>OK, sweetie. It's OK. It's OK, sweetie.
<v Woman>好的，亲爱的。没关系。没关系，亲爱的。

00:32:33.680 --> 00:32:37.630
<v Jeff>All right, we'll just do some banter. We'll do some banter.
<v Jeff>好的，我们做点闲聊。做点闲聊。

00:32:37.630 --> 00:32:39.690
<v Woman>Or we could ask Michael if he's ready.
<v Woman>或者我们可以问问迈克尔（Michael）他准备好了没。

00:32:39.690 --> 00:32:44.290
<v Michael>Yeah, I'm ready. I've been ready for this all year. I've been waiting for this opportunity all year.
<v Michael>对，我准备好了。我整年都在等待这个机会。

00:32:44.290 --> 00:32:47.960
<v Woman>Michael, I'm going to remind you of the ages of everybody in the family.
<v Woman>迈克尔，我要提醒你家里每个人的年龄。

00:32:47.960 --> 00:32:50.240
<v Michael>OK. OK.
<v Michael>好的。好的。

00:32:50.240 --> 00:32:50.850
<v Woman>All right, so--
<v Woman>好的，所以——

00:32:50.850 --> 00:32:57.600
<v Michael>Yeah, I'll remind you of my age. I'm 16, and I'm finally seeing the world for what it is, man. I'm finally seeing the world what it is. I'm 16, man.
<v Michael>对，我会提醒你我的年龄。我16岁了，我终于看清了这个世界，伙计。我终于看清了世界是什么样。我16岁了，伙计。

00:32:57.600 --> 00:32:58.320
<v Jeff>OK, Michael.
<v Jeff>好的，迈克尔。

00:32:58.320 --> 00:32:59.300
<v Woman>Michael, Michael.
<v Woman>迈克尔，迈克尔。

00:32:59.300 --> 00:33:00.280
<v Jeff>Michael, calm down.
<v Jeff>迈克尔，冷静点。

00:33:00.280 --> 00:33:00.600
<v Woman>Michael.
<v Woman>迈克尔。

00:33:00.600 --> 00:33:01.040
<v Michael>Yeah.
<v Michael>对。

00:33:01.040 --> 00:33:01.370
<v Jeff>Calm down.
<v Jeff>冷静点。

00:33:01.370 --> 00:33:01.710
<v Woman>Michael.
<v Woman>迈克尔。

00:33:01.710 --> 00:33:02.240
<v Michael>OK.
<v Michael>好的。

00:33:02.240 --> 00:33:03.130
<v Jeff>Calm down. Calm down.
<v Jeff>冷静点。冷静点。

00:33:03.130 --> 00:33:03.560
<v Woman>Michael, relax.
<v Woman>迈克尔，放松。

00:33:03.560 --> 00:33:06.830
<v Michael>I'm calm. Who's-- I'm calm. I'm calm!
<v Michael>我很冷静。谁——我很冷静。我很冷静！

00:33:06.830 --> 00:33:08.060
<v Woman>Uncurl your fists.
<v Woman>松开你的拳头。

00:33:08.060 --> 00:33:08.950
<v Michael>Who's yelling?
<v Michael>谁在叫？

00:33:08.950 --> 00:33:09.690
<v Woman>Uncurl your fists.
<v Woman>松开你的拳头。

00:33:09.690 --> 00:33:10.800
<v Michael>That's just how my hands are comfy.
<v Michael>我的手舒服就这样。

00:33:10.800 --> 00:33:13.030
<v Jeff>Hey.
<v Jeff>嘿。

00:33:13.030 --> 00:33:14.660
<v Michael>This is how my hands are comfortable.
<v Michael>我的手舒服就是这样。

00:33:14.660 --> 00:33:15.350
<v Woman>Michael?
<v Woman>迈克尔？

00:33:15.350 --> 00:33:16.300
<v Michael>What?
<v Michael>什么？

00:33:16.300 --> 00:33:17.840
<v Jeff>Are those brass knuckles?
<v Jeff>那是指虎吗？

00:33:17.840 --> 00:33:22.040
<v Michael>No, not if you don't hit anybody with them.
<v Michael>不，如果你不打人就不是。

00:33:22.040 --> 00:33:22.900
<v Jeff>Michael, put those away.
<v Jeff>迈克尔，把它收起来。

00:33:22.900 --> 00:33:24.320
<v Michael>They're just interconnected rings.
<v Michael>它们只是互锁的环。

00:33:24.320 --> 00:33:25.690
<v Woman>We--
<v Woman>我们——

00:33:25.690 --> 00:33:26.980
<v Boy>Can I have them? Can I have them?
<v Boy>能给我吗？能给我吗？

00:33:26.980 --> 00:33:28.610
<v Michael>Yeah, take them. Do whatever you want with them.
<v Michael>对，拿去。随便你怎么处置。

00:33:28.610 --> 00:33:31.360
<v Boy>Cool. (SINGING) Five golden rings.
<v Boy>酷。（歌唱）5个金戒指。

00:33:31.360 --> 00:33:36.850
<v Michael>Give them back. Give them back. Anything but that. Anything but that.
<v Michael>还给我。还给我。除了那个都可以。除了那个都可以。

00:33:36.850 --> 00:33:38.750
<v Michael>[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]
<v Michael>[观众笑声]

00:33:38.750 --> 00:33:50.200
<v Mike Birbiglia>I think one of the things that's really evocative about Christmas and childhood is actually fire. Like, we used to make fires.
<v Mike Birbiglia>我觉得圣诞节和童年最能引起共鸣的事情其实是火。就像，我们以前生火。

00:33:50.200 --> 00:33:52.450
<v Shasheer Zamata>What?
<v Shasheer Zamata>什么？

00:33:52.450 --> 00:33:57.860
<v Mike Birbiglia>In the fireplace, where one makes fire.
<v Mike Birbiglia>在壁炉里，人们生火的地方。

00:33:57.860 --> 00:34:01.590
<v Sasheer Zamata>You said "we" like every-- like it's a common experience.
<v Sasheer Zamata>你说的“我们”好像每个人——好像这是一种普遍的体验。

00:34:01.590 --> 00:34:06.850
<v Man>Like collectively we all associate Christmas with fire.
<v Man>好像集体地，我们都把圣诞节和火联系在一起。

00:34:06.850 --> 00:34:25.060
<v Aidy Bryant>I agree with Mike, where we always had like a big, beautiful fireplace where we would kind of gather around. But my parents remodeled their house when I was probably 11 a little bit. And they redid the fireplace, and it was like all these river rocks. Gorgeous, I know.
<v Aidy Bryant>我同意迈克的看法，我们一直有个巨大、漂亮的壁炉，我们可以聚在那里。但我父母在我11岁左右时重新装修了房子。他们重做了壁炉，全是河卵石。很华丽，我知道。

00:34:25.060 --> 00:34:51.320
<v Aidy Bryant>But they were, like, fake, you know? I mean, you couldn't tell that if you went, except for there's still to this day one at the very top that's deflated. It's like this deflated river rock. And so in all our Christmas pictures, it's all of us seated in front of the fireplace, and hanging above us is this weird, indented, sort of like light gray river rock.
<v Aidy Bryant>但它们是，假货，你知道吗？我是说，除非你走过去看，否则你分辨不出来，除了至今最上方还有一块是瘪的。就像这块瘪掉的河卵石。所以在我们所有的圣诞照片里，我们全家人坐在壁炉前，在我们上方悬挂着这块奇怪的、凹陷的、浅灰色的河卵石。

00:34:51.320 --> 00:34:54.280
<v Tami Sagher>Um, what's a river rock?
<v Tami Sagher>嗯，什么是河卵石？

00:34:54.280 --> 00:35:05.220
<v Aidy Bryant>Oh, I'm sorry. I was born and raised in the desert. So we're always searching for rivers. No, it's just-- they're like rounded rocks.
<v Aidy Bryant>噢，抱歉。我在沙漠长大。所以我们总是寻找河流。不，它只是——它们是像圆形的石头。

00:35:05.220 --> 00:35:08.790
<v Tami Sagher>So they couldn't get real ones? They had to get fake ones?
<v Tami Sagher>所以他们弄不到真的？非要弄假的？

00:35:08.790 --> 00:35:15.290
<v Aidy Bryant>Whoa, burn. Taking my family to task.
<v Aidy Bryant>哇，好毒的舌头。在指责我的家人。

00:35:15.290 --> 00:35:18.820
<v Sasheer Zamata>Also, is it full of air? Like, why is it deflated?
<v Sasheer Zamata>还有，里面是充满空气的吗？为什么它是瘪的？

00:35:18.820 --> 00:35:25.000
<v Aidy Bryant>Look, I didn't build it. I just-- I frickin' lived it.
<v Aidy Bryant>看，不是我建的。我只是——我该死地经历了它。

00:35:25.000 --> 00:35:27.980
<v Mom>Aidy, can you come here for a sec, sweetie?
<v Mom>艾迪，能过来一下吗，亲爱的？

00:35:27.980 --> 00:35:28.880
<v Aidy>Mm-hmm.
<v Aidy>嗯哼。

00:35:28.880 --> 00:35:30.950
<v Mom>Loved hearing you on the radio.
<v Mom>很高兴在广播里听到你。

00:35:30.950 --> 00:35:36.480
<v Aidy>OK.
<v Aidy>好的。

00:35:36.480 --> 00:35:47.180
<v Mom>I have to say, your dad and I got real sad though with what story you had to tell.
<v Mom>但我得说，你爸爸和我听了你的故事之后真的很伤心。

00:35:47.180 --> 00:35:54.190
<v Aidy>Um, I guess I-- I don't know. They chose that one. I did a ton of other nice stories.
<v Aidy>嗯，我想我——我不知道。他们选了那一个。我讲了很多其他温馨的故事。

00:35:54.190 --> 00:36:00.770
<v Mom>Did you talk about what happened when we gave you a four-foot St. Bernard stuffed toy?
<v Mom>你有没有提我们给你送了一个四英尺高的圣伯纳毛绒玩具时发生了什么？

00:36:00.770 --> 00:36:02.940
<v Mom>I'm going to stop this scene.
<v Mom>我要停下这个场景。

00:36:02.940 --> 00:36:13.890
<v Dad>Really, why? Why, you don't want to hear our opinions on how your hip, tight-pants friends don't like our rocks? Your hip friends with the tight pants?
<v Dad>真的，为什么？怎么，不想听我们评价你的那些穿紧身裤的朋友为什么不喜欢我们的石头吗？你那些穿着紧身裤的朋友们？

00:36:13.890 --> 00:36:17.450
<v Mom>They act like they don't know what a rock is.
<v Mom>他们装得好像不知道什么是石头。

00:36:17.450 --> 00:36:21.910
<v Dad>They act they like they don't know what a rock is. Oh, because you say "river," you don't know it's just a rock.
<v Dad>他们装得好像不知道什么是石头。噢，就因为你说了“河”，你就不知道那只是石头。

00:36:21.910 --> 00:36:24.370
<v Man>Hey, I heard your daughter on the radio.
<v Man>嘿，我在广播里听到你女儿的声音了。

00:36:24.370 --> 00:36:25.960
<v Dad>Yeah.
<v Dad>对。

00:36:25.960 --> 00:36:46.040
<v Man>We're avid-- Teresa and I are avid listeners to the public radio station here in Arizona. And it was very disappointing to hear that your family is an embarrassing family.
<v Man>对，特蕾莎（Teresa）和我是这里公共广播电台的忠实听众。听到你的家庭是个让人尴尬的家庭，真的很令人失望。

00:36:46.040 --> 00:36:51.340
<v Woman>Scene!
<v Woman>场景结束！

00:36:51.340 --> 00:37:16.340
<v Man>I will say the thing that was particularly special about Christmas-- because when I try to analyze what it is that made me experience this absolute euphoria in these two days is that my dad was there. My dad's a doctor, you know, which is wonderful. You know, he's a great doctor.
<v Man>我要说圣诞节特别特别的地方——因为当我尝试分析是什么让我在这两天体验到这种绝对的欣快时，是因为我爸爸在那儿。我爸爸是医生，你知道，这很棒。你知道，他是个伟大的医生。

00:37:16.340 --> 00:37:32.550
<v Man>But there would be no two days in the year for sure when I would know that he would be around for those two days. And it was like-- there was something where there was this joy of the full family that I'll never forget.
<v Man>但一年中绝对没有两天我会确定他会在家。这就像——那种全家团聚的快乐，我永生难忘。

00:37:32.550 --> 00:37:35.500
<v Man>Kids, kids, line up. Daddy's going to be here today. He's going to be here today.
<v Man>孩子们，孩子们，排好队。爸爸今天会在这里。他今天会在这里。

00:37:35.500 --> 00:37:38.110
<v Boy>Promise? You promise? There's nothing that could stop that, right?
<v Boy>承诺？你保证？没什么能阻止这一点，对吧？

00:37:38.110 --> 00:37:42.530
<v Man>No, he's coming. Today is the day. He wrote us. He told us. He phoned. Everything's all set.
<v Man>没，他会来。今天就是那一天。他写信给我们。他告诉我们了。他打电话了。一切都准备好了。

00:37:42.530 --> 00:37:50.250
<v Girl>Oh, man. I'm going to get love from him. I'm going to get advice from him. I'm going to get a spanking from them, because I've been bad.
<v Girl>噢，伙计。我要从他那儿得到爱。我要从他那儿得到建议。我要从他们那儿得到惩罚，因为我一直很淘气。

00:37:50.250 --> 00:37:57.180
<v Girl 2>I have so many questions to ask him that will shape how I view men.
<v Girl 2>我有太多问题要问他，这些将塑造我看待男人的方式。

00:37:57.180 --> 00:38:02.350
<v Boy>I'm just going to quietly observe him and then mimic him subtly forever.
<v Boy>我会静静地观察他，然后永远地模仿他。

00:38:02.350 --> 00:38:03.850
<v Girl 1>I'm so excited!
<v Girl 1>我太兴奋了！

00:38:03.850 --> 00:38:05.510
<v Boy>I can't wait!
<v Boy>我等不及了！

00:38:05.510 --> 00:38:06.830
<v Man>Oh, here he comes.
<v Man>噢，他来了。

00:38:06.830 --> 00:38:13.070
<v Girl 2>Oh, Dad!
<v Girl 2>噢，爸爸！

00:38:13.070 --> 00:38:14.320
<v Boy>Dad!
<v Boy>爸爸！

00:38:14.320 --> 00:38:23.510
<v Ira Glass>Kids. Tammy, Aidy, what's your name? Sasheer? Something with an S.
<v Ira Glass>孩子们。塔米，艾迪，你叫什么名字？萨希尔？以S开头的名字。

00:38:23.510 --> 00:38:28.620
<v Man>It's Samantha. I'm your wife.
<v Man>是萨曼莎。我是你妻子。

00:38:28.620 --> 00:38:33.030
<v Boy>Dad, Dad, look at my awards!
<v Boy>爸爸，爸爸，看我的奖状！

00:38:33.030 --> 00:38:35.520
<v Ira Glass>Very nice.
<v Ira Glass>非常好。

00:38:35.520 --> 00:38:43.620
<v Girl 1>Dad, spank me! I stole two years ago!
<v Girl 1>爸爸，打我屁股！我两年前偷东西了！

00:38:43.620 --> 00:38:47.190
<v Ira Glass>I just don't see why we have to go crazy like this. I don't see why we all have to go so crazy.
<v Ira Glass>我只是不明白我们为什么要像这样疯狂。我不明白为什么我们大家都得变得这么疯狂。

00:38:47.190 --> 00:38:48.090
<v Girl 2>Because we miss you!
<v Girl 2>因为我们想你！

00:38:48.090 --> 00:38:49.580
<v Boy>You're never around!
<v Boy>你从不在家！

00:38:49.580 --> 00:38:57.880
<v Girl 2>Dad, if I got all As, would you be around more? I've been throwing up, Dad.
<v Girl 2>爸爸，如果我拿了全A，你会多待一会儿吗？我一直吐，爸爸。

00:38:57.880 --> 00:39:04.720
<v Man>Don't they look good, though? Don't they look good? They look all clean, and they're posture is very good. Just like you like it. Just like you like it.
<v Man>它们看起来不错吧？它们看起来不错吧？看起来很整洁，姿势也很好。就像你喜欢的那样。就像你喜欢的那样。

00:39:04.720 --> 00:39:17.830
<v Boy>Dad, I appreciate that you work for Federal Express and that you guys will deliver packages 24 hours a day, seven days a week, 365 days a year.
<v Boy>爸爸，我很感激你为联邦快递（FedEx）工作，而且你们会一年365天、一天24小时、一周七天运送包裹。

00:39:17.830 --> 00:39:24.150
<v Girl 2>Plus you were on that island for a couple of years.
<v Girl 2>加上你在那个岛上待了几年。

00:39:24.150 --> 00:39:28.600
<v Boy>But you're just never around for us! We just want to hug you for an hour.
<v Boy>但你就是从来没时间陪我们！我们只想拥抱你一个小时。

00:39:28.600 --> 00:39:30.820
<v Man>Oh, my god. Don't say that out loud. Don't--
<v Man>噢，天哪。别大声说出来。别——

00:39:30.820 --> 00:39:38.210
<v Ira Glass>I just think that-- you just need to understand that I love you all, but I'm just very busy, just very, very busy--
<v Ira Glass>我只是觉得——你只需要明白我爱你们所有人，但我只是很忙，只是非常、非常忙——

00:39:38.210 --> 00:39:40.620
<v Man>Oh, let them hug you, please.
<v Man>噢，让他们拥抱你，拜托。

00:39:40.620 --> 00:39:50.270
<v Girl 1>No, it's OK, Mom. Dad's too busy for a hug.
<v Girl 1>没，没关系，妈妈。爸爸太忙了，没空拥抱。

00:39:50.270 --> 00:39:52.680
<v Man>Thomas, look at their faces.
<v Man>托马斯（Thomas），看看他们的脸。

00:39:52.680 --> 00:39:57.530
<v Girl 2>It's OK, Mom. I don't deserve to be touched.
<v Girl 2>没关系，妈妈。我不配被触碰。

00:39:57.530 --> 00:40:03.980
<v Girl 3>Sometimes I just send an empty package, hoping that you'll bring it back.
<v Girl 3>有时候我只是寄个空包裹，希望你会带回来。

00:40:03.980 --> 00:40:10.390
<v Girl 3>[AUDIENCE LAUGHS]
<v Girl 3>[观众笑声]

00:40:10.390 --> 00:40:18.860
<v Boy>Dad, I just want you to know I can sense the emotional distance you're keeping. And someday I plan on replicating and furthering it.
<v Boy>爸爸，我只是想让你知道我能感觉到你保持的情感距离。总有一天我计划复制并进一步加深它。

00:40:18.860 --> 00:40:21.090
<v Ira Glass>All right. I'll see you all next year.
<v Ira Glass>好的。明年见。

00:40:21.090 --> 00:40:22.470
<v Boy>Oh. Dad.
<v Boy>噢。爸爸。

00:40:22.470 --> 00:40:23.130
<v Man>There he goes.
<v Man>他走了。

00:40:23.130 --> 00:40:37.430
<v Boy>You know what I just noticed, Dad? It's like you're inverse Santa Claus. Like, Santa Claus brings kids packages one day a year, and then you never see him again. And we only see you today, and then you bring people packages every other day.
<v Boy>你知道我刚才注意到什么吗，爸爸？你就像反向圣诞老人。就像，圣诞老人一年给孩子们送一次包裹，然后你就再也见不到他了。而我们今天才见到你，然后你剩下的日子里每天都给人们送包裹。

00:40:37.430 --> 00:40:52.740
