<v Stephanie Foo>I saw in the "up next column" in YouTube that there were more videos like this, turkey fryer fire safety PSAs put out by fire departments across the country. We stopped counting at 150 videos. They come from Tucson to Pensacola to Danville, California, all made to demonstrate the dangers of deep frying. A lot of the videos were clearly done as segments for local TV stations.
<v Stephanie Foo>我在YouTube的“下一个视频”栏里看到还有更多这样的视频，那是全国各地的消防部门发布的炸火鸡安全公告。我们在第150个视频时停止了计数。它们来自图森、彭萨科拉到加利福尼亚的丹维尔，全是用来演示深炸带来的危险。很多视频显然是作为当地电视台的板块制作的。

00:44:42.770 --> 00:44:48.650
<v Stephanie Foo>But some departments employ different theatrical methods to amp up the drama on the PSAs. Some use slow mo.
<v Stephanie Foo>但一些部门采用了不同的戏剧手法来增加公告的戏剧性。一些使用了慢动作。

00:44:48.650 --> 00:44:51.040
<v Stephanie Foo>[OIL SLOWLY SIZZLING]
<v Stephanie Foo>[慢动作的油滋滋声]

00:44:51.040 --> 00:44:54.900
<v Stephanie Foo>Some play epic music as you watch closeups of the pot of oil.
<v Stephanie Foo>一些在你看特写镜头时播放史诗般的音乐。

